              Organizations and Manufactured Transparency
              in the Age of Surveillance
            </h2>

            <p class="paper-description">
              This project investigates how organizations respond when their surveillance practices become contested.
              In ongoing work, I track how agencies navigate public scrutiny by selectively disclosing information about their use of surveillance technologies, 
              manufacturing an artificial appearance of transparency while obscuring the full scope of their practices.
